Feature: OrderService
  @owner: "orders"

Description:
  Places and cancels customer orders; settlement is derived from
  the placed order, never dispatched by hand.

Relationships:
  EmitsTo: PaymentProcessing with events="order.created"

Scenario: Placing an order drives settlement
  @smoke, @saga
  When an order is placed
  Then events "order.created", "payment.settled" are emitted
    And commands "order.create", "payment.settle" are dispatched

Scenario: Placing a second order is rejected
  @error
  Given a placed order
  When an order is placed
  Then the command is rejected because the order already exists

Scenario: Cancelling a placed order
  @read-model
  Given a placed order
  When the order is cancelled
  Then the order is cancelled in the read model

Scenario: Cancelling an unknown order is rejected
  @error
  When the order is cancelled
  Then the command is rejected because the order does not exist

Scenario: The read model sees the settlement
  @read-model
  When an order is placed
  Then commands "order.create", "payment.settle" are dispatched
    And the settled stage count is 1

Feature: PaymentProcessing
  @owner: "payments"

Description:
  Settles placed orders. The payment.settle command is DERIVED from
  order.created by the bus deriver (ADR-0154); only the read model
  and the event journal ever see settlement happen.

Relationships:
  ListensFrom: OrderService with events="order.created"
  EmitsTo: Fulfillment with events="payment.settled"

Feature: Fulfillment
  @owner: "logistics"

Description:
  Ships settled orders. Docs-only in this fixture: the feature graph
  and the EventCatalog flows describe the dependency, no executable
  scenarios yet.

Relationships:
  ListensFrom: PaymentProcessing with events="payment.settled"
  ProvidesTo: OrderService
